WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.463
Now, which cloud.

2
00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:06.428
The callback goes to Microsoft Graph,
and the host depends on the tenant:

3
00:00:06.428 --> 00:00:11.646
a GCC tenant like this estate's keeps
the worldwide endpoint, while GCC High

4
00:00:11.646 --> 00:00:16.612
and DoD each have their own, and a token
for one cloud won't work in another.

5
00:00:16.612 --> 00:00:18.601
The Logic App's side matters too.

6
00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:23.038
Learn documents the proof-of-possession
policy only for commercial Azure.

7
00:00:23.038 --> 00:00:27.850
For Azure Government it gives nothing, so
the builder refuses rather than guess.

8
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:31.792
Licensing and availability are
covered in all the US clouds,

9
00:00:31.792 --> 00:00:34.788
and the tenant limits
are the same everywhere.

10
00:00:34.788 --> 00:00:37.060
Next, Microsoft's own sample.
